;;; `open` written as a conclusion's argument loads, and a rule derives a fact
;;; about it — M1f **W71**, register row `W71/conclusion-value`, filed by
;;; S1f.5.23 (T1f.5.23.2, 2026-11-10).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `r` concludes `(p open)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is the verdict a rule's `:assert` states, `(open)` or `(open ?R)`,
;;; and is written nowhere else (the user's ruling on Q-M1f.66, 2026-11-10):
;;; here it is written as a conclusion's argument, so the program is refused at
;;; the parse, at the `open`, and every command exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, root derives `(p open)`, and R is
;;; 16 states, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at the parse since S1f.5.23 (T1f.5.23.3).

(relation a Thing :why "{?1} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?1} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?1} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(rule r ()
  :match  (a ?x)
  :assert (p open)
  :why "{?x} is an a, so open is a p")
